{"record":{"actor":"codex","at":1793472657,"body":{"commit":"086c25144b1fcbdb9c5aecf5937fb73cbe806d0e","severity":"P2","statement":"P2 Witness one R-R step rather than only the final REF-chain receipt","target":"7d20fb0afbf1ef160e78fa40d3f954359e087dadd81ae371f89f64282b193032","test":{"case":"F1","file":"book1_rr_claim_binding_test","patch":"--- /dev/null\n+++ b/tests/book1_rr_claim_binding_test.py\n@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"F1: the witness of exactly-one-level R-R must reject a two-level step.\"\"\"\n+import contextlib\n+import io\n+import runpy\n+import sys\n+from pathlib import Path\n+from unittest.mock import patch\n+\n+ROOT = Path.cwd()\n+sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"impl\"))\n+import sigma_glyph as sg\n+\n+\n+def witnesses():\n+    output = io.StringIO()\n+    code = 0\n+    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(output):\n+        try:\n+            runpy.run_path(str(ROOT / \"tests/book1_claims_test.py\"), run_name=\"__main__\")\n+        except SystemExit as exc:\n+            code = exc.code\n+    return code, output.getvalue()\n+\n+\n+code, output = witnesses()\n+if code != 0 or not any(line.startswith(\"ok   B111 \") for line in output.splitlines()):\n+    print(\"FAIL F1 baseline B111 is not green\")\n+    sys.exit(1)\n+\n+real_step = sg.step5\n+fused = []\n+\n+\n+def two_level_step(term, remaining, store, stats, limits):\n+    if term[0] == \"ref\":\n+        data = store.get(term[1])\n+        node = sg.deser(data) if data else None\n+        if node and node[\"op\"] == sg.REF:\n+            # Fuse R-R (1), next REF materialization (2), and its R-R (1).\n+            # Final hash and total ATP stay unchanged; one step skips a level.\n+            sg._require_budget(4, remaining)\n+            target = sg.force(term[1], store, stats, limits)\n+            fused.append(True)\n+            return (\"thunk\", target[1]), 4\n+    return real_step(term, remaining, store, stats, limits)\n+\n+\n+with patch.object(sg, \"step5\", two_level_step):\n+    mutant_code, mutant_output = witnesses()\n+\n+rejected = any(line.startswith(\"FAIL B111 \") for line in mutant_output.splitlines())\n+if fused and not rejected:\n+    print(\"FAIL F1 B111 accepts two REF levels in one step (witness exit \" + str(mutant_code) + \")\")\n+    sys.exit(1)\n+print(\"ok   F1 B111 rejects two REF levels in one step\")\n"},"tree":"0a4381f0b9f5defe5c02ffc4492db058f40596c7","what":"BOOK1-3.1-4 quotes the MUST that R-R unwraps exactly one level per step, but B111 observes only the final hash and aggregate 6 ATP. Its G11 mutant changes the price from 1 to 0 while still unwrapping exactly one level, so it does not contradict that quoted claim. A counter-stepper that fuses R-R + materialization of the next REF + R-R into one action charged 4 ATP skips the required intermediate thunk and still passes all 17 witnesses, including B111. The attached regression reproduces this at X without editing the oracle: it monkeypatches step5 with that two-level contraction. Strengthening B111 with a direct single-step assertion makes the regression pass. Assert the intermediate thunk, cost and absence of extra resolution, and cite a mutant that actually collapses REF levels (or narrow the backed claim to what the witness establishes). This is a gap in the new claim evidence, not an observed defect in the unmodified oracle.","where":["tests/book1_claims_test.py:114","tests/claims_mutants.py:39"]},"guard":null,"kind":"challenge","lineage":null,"prev":"c0e8a7620b582546c693e1453589a64c5d9456c9d48b7086c9b878143ec92b9f","refs":["7d20fb0afbf1ef160e78fa40d3f954359e087dadd81ae371f89f64282b193032"],"schema":"finding@1","warrant":"3"},"sig":{"ed25519":"3375c287b9ff754abff67e94da4eaf2de90de96e00e0ce057b66b85e8aa52890143511bd7780a6ec73c93b3f5a219cdf4999a04c2fb7172771c41b5611986305","key":"fbe15554075e09d3be6c29344143a0f1700a44f0150f9a0bf208cc8bced5f798"}}
